I walk over to the register with my new things.
The clerk looks up and says hi.
"Hi," she says.
"Hi," I reply.
I put the light green jacket and the blue shirt on the counter.
She scans both things in.
"That will be six hundred and fifty kroner," she says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you want the receipt?" the clerk asks.
"Yes please," I answer quickly.
"I have not tried the shirt on," I explain.
"I hope I won't need a bigger one."
"You can always exchange it," the clerk says kindly.
She prints the receipt out and gives it to me.
"Remember to save it," she says.
I take the receipt.
I fold the small piece of paper.
Then I put it safely down into my wallet.
"Have a good weekend," I say to her.
"You too," she replies.
